anyone who's ever used a Mercedes  Sprinter for a move knows just how much  furniture can fit inside but this heimer  car isn't your standard multipurpose  Sprinter it's a fully equipped camper  van that was developed by heimer and  Mercedes designed to meet your every  need while on holiday our car tester  Michelle Assenmacher is trying out the  Grand Canyon s it's based on the  Mercedes Sprinter and has tailor-made  furniture from heimer  the vehicle is five point nine three  meters long and seats four people the  seats can be arranged around a table  there's plenty of storage space thanks  to the many cupboards but the vehicle  never seems cramped due to a  well-designed interior in all open  amenities we all tend to take lots of  stuff on holiday but there are enough  drawers for storing everything but to  ensure nothing goes flying around the  van while driving the drawers come with  special catches to lock them all you  need to do is push the buttons on Shawn  come it's a posse on the Grand Canyon s  has also fitted with a small kitchen so  no one needs to go hungry there's a hob  with two rings under this cover and a  small sink  and there's a tall fridge besides the  kitchen unit offering plenty of space  console and of course no campervan is  complete without a toilet and a shower  they're located here the basin is fitted  onto the side wall and can be folded  away to save space it comes with a  pull-out water tap that can also be used  for showering the show points out  there's a shower curtain to prevent  everything from getting wet what more  could you ask for  the Grand Canyon s also comes with comfy  mattresses unlike many other camper vans  where seating areas double up as beds  Darren can see the Grand Canyon has is  cleverly laid out Michele demonstrates  another space-saving feature  the Vans rear can be quickly transformed  into a cozy bed for two and in  summertime you can look through the rear  doors onto the sea while you're nodding  off  Conestoga Alto Samia blinking on table  and fluffy  Michelle likes the Grand Canyon s a lot  she finds regular campervans just too  big for people her age but this smaller  van is really to her liking tough the  non language market and so there's a  campervan for every taste smaller and  more agile vans like this one are  beginning to match up to the bigger ones  in terms of features and they weigh less  so in many countries no special driver's  license is necessary
 

